 command whose own row ranks in the same result (`BRIDGE_COMMAND_BY_ID` and `alreadyOffered` in `enrichCompiledRoutes`). The option `compiledRouteTopOnly` exists. Neither is planned again.\n175: - The CLI hook path keeps `command` (`recommendationFromCli` in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`) and retries once without a rejected option for an older daemon (`invokeAdvisorRecommendPayload` and `COMPILED_ROUTE_OPTION_KEYS` in `ADV/skill-advisor-cli.ts`).\n176: - The doctor runnable string with its route target, such as `/doctor:git hooks`, is generated into `DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS` (`ADV/lib/render.ts`) by `renderDoctorCommandStrings` (`ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`). That covers the L6 runnable string for doctor rows.\n177: - One policy per command and per doctor route is generated as `commandPolicies` by `derivePolicy` and `commandPolicies` in the deriver.\n178: - The TypeScript hand-authored array is gone from `ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts`, and all 62 generated rows set `routingEnabled` (45 true, 17 false).\n179: - The allow-list holds 4 rows, not 8. `/spec_kit`, `/memory:save`, `/prompt` and the umbrella `command-spec-kit` have no allow-list row, and `AGENTS.md` names none of the retired ids.\n180: - No two TypeScript-enabled rows share a runnable string (counted from the generated file).\n181: \n182: ### What Is Missing\n183: - `kind`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` on the public recommendation, and `command` on a command row's own entry.\n184: - A brief label for any non-doctor command row and any attached command. Today the head prints the raw id or the hub skill alone.\n185: - A policy for `/doctor:update`, whose bridge names no action while its six actions carry three different policies.\n186: - A stated contract for a degraded result. The local Python scorer returns `command-create-readme` as a passing row for a plain prompt.\n187: - The four allow-list ids, the Python `\"/prompt\"` lexical row and owner branch, the two Python hand-authored constants and the optional `routingEnabled` type.\n188: - An owner-aware hit in the router vocabulary reach check. Without it the check fails on `sk-doc` with real embeddings on, because a meaning-passed command that `sk-doc` owns ranks first.\n189: <!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n190: \n191: ---\n192: \n193: <!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n194: ## 3. SCOPE\n195: \n196: ### In Scope\n197: - Generate one table `COMMAND_ROWS` in `ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, keyed by every id a scorer can return for a command entry, holding its runnable `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId`, plus `COMMAND_POLICIES` keyed by runnable string. It replaces the doctor-only `DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS`.\n198: - Add `kind`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` to the public recommendation and fill all four fields from that table in the handler, the CLI fallback and the renderer.\n199: - Render the brief head as `use <owner> → <command> (<policy>)` for a recommendation that names a command, with no consequence line (L12).\n200: - State and test the degraded contract on the CLI's `degraded: true` path.\n201: - Retire the allow-list file, its four ids and the Python `/prompt` residue, delete the Python hand-authored constants and make `routingEnabled` required (L7).\n202: - Make `nm-sk-doc-01` route to `sk-doc` by correcting the routing signal at its source, never by a phrase copied from its prompt.\n203: - Make `rankShippedFleet` in `ci-router-vocabulary-reach.cjs` count a winning command row whose `ownerSkillId` is the probed hub as a hit.\n204: - CARRY-003: clear the typed `/create:agent` ambiguity, prove that a metadata command with no compatibility row is active and reach `/speckit:search` from the review's probe prompt.\n205: \n206: ### Out of Scope\n207: - Raising the brief token cap. The research eliminated it, and the new head fits 80 tokens.\n208: - A consequence line or argument state in the brief (L6, L12). The command's own setup asks for its arguments.\n209: - An `argumentHint` field. No current caller reads it, and the operator answered no.\n210: - Changing a policy, a risk class or a scoring weight. Phase 002 owns the policies, and the four pinned numbers are a floor.\n211: - The `Also:` companion line. It keeps its doctor-only trigger and its runnable label.\n212: - `AGENTS.md`, the Gate 2 sentence and the runtime pointers. Phase 006 owns them.\n213: - The Python-only ids `command-spec-kit-deep-research` and `command-spec-kit-deep-review`, the TypeScript compatibility ids `create:agent` and `create:manual-testing-playbook`, and the alias folds that map old ids onto live ones. The operator chose to rename only the four allow-list ids.\n214: - Typed `/memory:save` as prompt vocabulary in `explicit.ts`, `fusion.ts`, the Python scorer and the Gate 3 classifier. It matches what a user types, and five labelled corpus rows type it.\n215: \n216: ### Files to Change\n217: \n218: | File Path | Change Type | Description |\n219: |-----------|-------------|-------------|\n220: | `ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` | Modify | Emit `COMMAND_ROWS` and `COMMAND_POLICIES`, stop emitting the doctor block, stop reading the allow-list |\n221: | `ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` | Modify | The generated block and `commandRowFor` |\n222: | `ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` | Modify | `kind`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` on the recommendation |\n223: | `ADV/lib/subprocess.ts` | Modify | Optional `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` on `AdvisorRecommendation` |\n224: | `ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` | Modify | Fill the fields, and give an attached command its policy |\n225: | `ADV/lib/render.ts` | Modify | The new head label, the doctor block removed |\n226: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | Modify | Keep `kind`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` |\n227: | `ADV/skill-advisor-cli.ts` | Modify | The degraded contract in `degradedRecommendations` |\n228: | `ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` | Modify | `routingEnabled` required, regenerated block |\n229: | `ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py` | Modify | Hand constants and `/prompt` residue deleted, four ids re-pointed |\n230: | `ADV/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json` | Delete | Its four rows come from `system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json` |\n231: | `ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json` | Modify | Four Python rows and one owner key deleted |\n232: | `ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts`, `ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`, `ADV/lib/scorer/scoring-constants.ts` | Modify | Re-point `command-spec-kit-resume` and `command-spec-kit-plan` |\n233: | Gold and fixture files listed in the measured block | Modify | Relabel the four ids by script, without reading prompt text |\n234: | The one routing source file the `nm-sk-doc-01` trace names | Modify | One signal corrected at its source |\n235: | `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.cjs`, `scripts/tests/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.test.cjs` | Modify | Owner-aware hit and two fixture cases |\n236: | `ADV/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json` | Modify | CARRY-003 (a) and (c) |\n237: | Tests under `ADV/tests/` | Create, Modify | Schema, golden briefs, degraded contract, old daemon, CARRY-003 (b) |\n238: | `hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`, `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`, `ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md` | Modify | The fields, the brief form and the degraded contract |\n239: <!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n240: \n241: ---\n242: \n243: <!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n244: ## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n245: REQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n246: \n247: ### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n248: \n249: | ID | Requirement |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 250]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/spec.md\",\"offset\":140,\"limit\":110}"},"time":{"start":1794522509298,"end":1794522510078}}}}
