{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794522807372,"sessionID":"ses_e2e22251effedzgdgxW9ZYGzGw","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1e4e254002DuYeFWjazQvwrF","sessionID":"ses_e2e22251effedzgdgxW9ZYGzGw","messageID":"msg_1d1e4a8fc001U3xpzXtneqOdfA","type":"tool","id":"call_f1c9100b1168434ba3759d02","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/scratch/nm-sk-doc-source.txt","content":"# nm-sk-doc-01 token source trace\n\nDate: 2026-11-12\nInput: scratch/nm-sk-doc-before.txt, probe prompt \"fix the typo in the heading of the setup guide\"\nCode read: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/lexical.ts` and `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts`\n\n## How a skill's token list is built\n\n`scoreLexicalLane` builds each skill's candidate strings from `id`, `name`, `description`, `domains`, `intentSignals` and `keywords`. It scores them with `scoreTokenOverlap` and harvests `token:<x>` evidence with a plain `haystack.includes(token)` over the same joined candidates.\n`projectionFromRow` fills `name`, `description` and `keywords` from the skill's `SKILL.md` through `parseSkillMarkdown`, and `domains` and `intentSignals` from the `skill_nodes` row. `indexSkillMetadata` reads that row from the skill's `graph-metadata.json` fields `domains` and `intent_signals`, so an edit to `graph-metadata.json` reaches the SQLite projection only after a re-index.\n\n## Token sources\n\ntypo | sk-code | .skilled/skills/sk-code/graph-metadata.json | field domains | \"typography\" gives token:typo by substring only, while scoreTokenOverlap tokenizes and does not score typo against typography\nheading | sk-code | .skilled/skills/sk-code/graph-metadata.json | field intent_signals | \"text-wrap balance headings\" gives token:heading by substring and scores 0.45 through the heading to headings suffix extension\nguide | sk-design | .skilled/skills/sk-design/graph-metadata.json | field intent_signals | \"style guide from\" and \"style guide from a url\" give token:guide as an exact token\nsetup | system-skilled-doctor | .skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/graph-metadata.json | field intent_signals | \"doctor setup\", \"doctor setup diagnostic\" and \"what doctor setup prints\" give token:setup. The separate derived:setup evidence comes from field derived.key_files, \".skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\" reduced to \"setup\"\ndebug | sk-code | .skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md | field description | \"Implement, debug and verify code...\" gives token:debug as an exact token. The same token is also in the SKILL.md Keywords block and in graph-metadata.json intent_signals \"debug the ci\"\n\n## Why sk-doc holds no documentation-edit token\n\n`sk-doc` projects documentation artifacts and authoring actions (`documentation`, `markdown`, `authoring`, `readme`, `feature catalog`, `frontmatter`, `create`, `validate`, `review the docs`) but no term for editing existing prose, such as typo, heading, spelling, proofread or wording. The prompt's scorable tokens are `fix`, `typo`, `heading`, `setup` and `guide`, plus the synonyms `debug`, `correct` and `patch` that `fix` injects. None is a whole token in `sk-doc`'s candidate strings. The only literal \"fix\" sits inside \"fixture\" in `intent_signals` (\"benchmark fixture\" and \"reviewer-prompt fixture\"). Scoring is whole-token, so the 3-letter prompt token `fix` does not match `fixture`, `sk-doc` scores 0, and `scoreLexicalLane` drops a row at score <= 0.05 before it can harvest evidence. That is why `sk-doc` carries no token and never enters the recommendation list.\n\n## sk-doc source field that should carry documentation-edit vocabulary\n\nsk-doc source field: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json -> intent_signals\n"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/scratch/nm-sk-doc-source.txt","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/scratch/nm-sk-doc-source.txt"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/scratch/nm-sk-doc-source.txt\",\"content\":\"# nm-sk-doc-01 token source trace\\n\\nDate: 2026-11-12\\nInput: scratch/nm-sk-doc-before.txt, probe prompt \\\"fix the typo in the heading of the setup guide\\\"\\nCode read: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/lexical.ts` and `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts`\\n\\n## How a skill's token list is built\\n\\n`scoreLexicalLane` builds each skill's candidate strings from `id`, `name`, `description`, `domains`, `intentSignals` and `keywords`. It scores them with `scoreTokenOverlap` and harvests `token:<x>` evidence with a plain `haystack.includes(token)` over the same joined candidates.\\n`projectionFromRow` fills `name`, `description` and `keywords` from the skill's `SKILL.md` through `parseSkillMarkdown`, and `domains` and `intentSignals` from the `skill_nodes` row. `indexSkillMetadata` reads that row from the skill's `graph-metadata.json` fields `domains` and `intent_signals`, so an edit to `graph-metadata.json` reaches the SQLite projection only after a re-index.\\n\\n## Token sources\\n\\ntypo | sk-code | .skilled/skills/sk-code/graph-metadata.json | field domains | \\\"typography\\\" gives token:typo by substring only, while scoreTokenOverlap tokenizes and does not score typo against typography\\nheading | sk-code | .skilled/skills/sk-code/graph-metadata.json | field intent_signals | \\\"text-wrap balance headings\\\" gives token:heading by substring and scores 0.45 through the heading to headings suffix extension\\nguide | sk-design | .skilled/skills/sk-design/graph-metadata.json | field intent_signals | \\\"style guide from\\\" and \\\"style guide from a url\\\" give token:guide as an exact token\\nsetup | system-skilled-doctor | .skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/graph-metadata.json | field intent_signals | \\\"doctor setup\\\", \\\"doctor setup diagnostic\\\" and \\\"what doctor setup prints\\\" give token:setup. The separate derived:setup evidence comes from field derived.key_files, \\\".skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\\\" reduced to \\\"setup\\\"\\ndebug | sk-code | .skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md | field description | \\\"Implement, debug and verify code...\\\" gives token:debug as an exact token. The same token is also in the SKILL.md Keywords block and in graph-metadata.json intent_signals \\\"debug the ci\\\"\\n\\n## Why sk-doc holds no documentation-edit token\\n\\n`sk-doc` projects documentation artifacts and authoring actions (`documentation`, `markdown`, `authoring`, `readme`, `feature catalog`, `frontmatter`, `create`, `validate`, `review the docs`) but no term for editing existing prose, such as typo, heading, spelling, proofread or wording. The prompt's scorable tokens are `fix`, `typo`, `heading`, `setup` and `guide`, plus the synonyms `debug`, `correct` and `patch` that `fix` injects. None is a whole token in `sk-doc`'s candidate strings. The only literal \\\"fix\\\" sits inside \\\"fixture\\\" in `intent_signals` (\\\"benchmark fixture\\\" and \\\"reviewer-prompt fixture\\\"). Scoring is whole-token, so the 3-letter prompt token `fix` does not match `fixture`, `sk-doc` scores 0, and `scoreLexicalLane` drops a row at score <= 0.05 before it can harvest evidence. That is why `sk-doc` carries no token and never enters the recommendation list.\\n\\n## sk-doc source field that should carry documentation-edit vocabulary\\n\\nsk-doc source field: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json -> intent_signals\\n\"}"},"time":{"start":1794522800724,"end":1794522807372}}}}
